<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Paris Peace Agreements</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1991">1991</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Paris Peace Accords on Cambodia, Paris Peace Agreements (1991), Paris Peace Accords (1991) · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodian-vietnamese-war">Cambodian–Vietnamese War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> Peace Agreements were signed on 23 October 1991 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a>'s Supreme National Council, representing the rival factions, and eighteen other states to end the war in Cambodia that followed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>'s invasion of 1978. They provided for a ceasefire, the disarming of the factions and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> transitional authority, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations-transitional-authority-in-cambodia">UNTAC</a>, which organised elections in 1993.</p></div>
